<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="k" from="7" to="9" step="1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="b" from="75" to="90" step="5"/>

  <function name="v" variable="t">$b-$k*t</function>
  <function name="s" variable="t">$b*t-$k*t^2/2</function>

</setup>

<p>
  Suppose that a car is braking to a stop.  When it starts braking, its velocity is <m>$b</m> feet per second, and it brakes in such a way that its velocity decreases at a constant rate of <m>$k</m> feet per second per second.
</p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        Find a formula for the car's velocity at an arbitrary time <m>t</m> between the time it starts braking and when its velocity reaches <m>0</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer><label><m>v(t) = </m> </label>$v</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        How long does it take for the car to come to a complete stop?
      </p>
      <p>
        The car stops when <answer name="tEntered" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.0001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><label><m>t = </m> </label>$b/$k</answer> seconds.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        How far does the car travel between the time it starts braking and when it stops?  Report your result accurate to at least 4 decimal places.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><mathInput name="dEntered"><label>distance traveled while braking is </label></mathInput><award><when>$dEntered=$$s($tEntered) and $tEntered.creditAchieved=1</when></award></answer> with units <answer><choiceInput inline>
          <shortDescription>options for units</shortDescription>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>feet per second</choice>
          <choice credit="1">feet</choice>
          <choice>seconds</choice>
        </choiceInput></answer>.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>